# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages. Hifth routes via the URL hash (spec §7), so
# the path is always the app root; any non-asset path resolves to index.html
# with a 200 so a cold deep-link boots the app, which then reads the hash.
#
# Read by Cloudflare ONLY, and — because of that first sentence — the reason the
# default host needed no equivalent. GitHub Pages has no rewrite rules at all,
# which rules out a history-routed SPA and would have made this deploy a code
# change. Hash routing means a deep link like /hifth/#/hafs/p7 requests the
# directory index and nothing else, so there is nothing to fall back *from*.
# A convention chosen for share links (a teacher pastes one, it cold-opens on
# the exact view) turned out to decide which hosts Hifth can be served from.
/*  /index.html  200
